        name: "style-feature-name",
        prose: "A container style query allows querying the computed values of the query container. It is a boolean combination of individual style features (<style-feature>) that each query a single, specific property of the query container. The syntax of a <style-feature> is either the same as for a valid declaration[CSS-SYNTAX-3], a <style-feature-name> or a valid style range (<style-range>). The <style-feature-name> can be either a supported CSS property or a valid <custom-property-name>. The <style-feature-value> production matches any valid <declaration-value> as long as it doesn\u2019t contain <mf-lt>, <mf-gt> and <mf-eq> tokens.",
